From 1e00314553594d9bf0f8174ae6e15b28f3bcf7c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 14:10:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: keep the last character of monster messages without [|]

borg_get_parsed_pain() copies a monster message into a buffer that starts
with an added space, so the buffer needs room for the space, the text and
the terminator.  It allocated strlen + 1 bytes, which is enough only when
the text contains "[singular|plural]" markup that is dropped while
copying.  For a message without that markup the last character was cut
off, so " can move again.", " falls under your spell!",
" is no longer under your control." and " shimmers for a moment." were
stored without their final '.' or '!' and never matched the message the
game prints.  The borg then ignored those lines instead of noting them
against the monster, as it does for "is no longer stunned." and the
other monster status messages.

Allocate strlen + 2 bytes.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#197.

(cherry picked from commit 8a0c13f7127642da8222c84380b4e6b8f9f96eff)
---
 src/borg/borg-messages.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-messages.c b/src/borg/borg-messages.c
index 8132cd56a..fb44d4de0 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-messages.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-messages.c
@@ -1628,7 +1628,8 @@ static void borg_init_spell_messages(void)
 /* load monster in pain messages */
 static char *borg_get_parsed_pain(const char *pain, bool do_plural)
 {
-    size_t buflen = strlen(pain) + 1;
+    /* Room for the leading space, the text and the terminator */
+    size_t buflen = strlen(pain) + 2;
     char  *buf    = mem_zalloc(buflen);
 
     int    state  = MSG_PARSE_NORMAL;
